th. I can do one glob with pattern \"{todo.md,sum.txt}\"? Glob brace support — likely supported by the glob library. Or two globs in parallel. Let me do two globs in one block, then two writes in one block.\n\nActually, simpler: just check with a single glob \"*\" — that lists up to 100 files in the workspace. That tells me if either exists. Then write both in parallel. If the directory is empty, both are new files.\n\nThen after writes, done. Report: sum = 5050, show the formula, mention both files written in parallel. No present needed — these are plain text files, final response suffices. Actually present is for separate deliverables... text files could be presented but guidance says prefer final response when it suffices. These are simple; I'll just mention them with links. The guidance: link every mention of an existing file to its full path relative to working directory. So [todo.md](todo.md) and [sum.txt](sum.txt).\n\nsum.txt content — the calculation process in Chinese:\n```\n1 + 2 + 3 + ... + 100\n配对求和（高斯法）：\n  1 + 100 = 101\n  2 + 99 = 101\n  3 + 98 = 101\n  ...\n  50 + 51 = 101\n共 50 对，每对和为 101\n总和 = 101 × 50 = 5050\n```\n\nGood. Let me execute."}}}}
